  "id": "reference-distribution",
  "term": "reference distribution",
  "definition": "A reference distribution is a comparison distribution used to judge whether the heights of branch points in a hierarchical clustering dendrogram are unlikely to have occurred by chance. In this context, it provides the basis for assigning a significance level when choosing where to cut the dendrogram into groups.",
